7. System Architecture: The Spectral Governor

The preceding mathematics compels a new operational role: the Collective Intelligence Architect reconceived as a Spectral Governor—an entity (human + AI support) that continuously monitors and enforces the spectral envelope.

7.1 Core Processes

1. Real-Time Spectrum Monitoring. The CIA maintains a live digital twin of the multiplex  \mathcal{M} , updated from communication logs, delegation records, and training assessments. Eigenvalues  \lambda_2, \rho(A), \gamma  are recomputed on a rolling basis.
2. Perturbation Pre-approval. Any proposed change—personnel rotation, introduction of an AI summariser, restructuring of working groups—must be submitted as a topological change proposal. The CIA computes the expected shifts  \Delta \lambda_2, \Delta \rho(A), \Delta \mathcal{D}  using a perturbation-theoretic linear approximation:
   \Delta \lambda_2 \approx \mathbf{v}_2^\top (\Delta \mathcal{L}) \mathbf{v}_2,
   where  \mathbf{v}_2  is the Fiedler vector of the current Laplacian. If any invariant would leave  \Lambda_{\text{safe}} , the proposal is vetoed.
3. Control Responses.
   · If  \lambda_2 < \epsilon_{\text{crit}} : trigger edge addition by scheduling cross-domain “bridge” assignments.
   · If  \rho(A) > \rho_{\text{threshold}} : insert human-in-the-loop audit gates into AI delegation paths, effectively reducing edge weights.
   · If  \mathcal{D} > \tau : activate “topology restoration” protocols that rewire the network toward the reference structure.
4. Redundancy Basis Monitoring. Using the Gram matrix  G , the CIA computes the effective redundancy  R_{\text{eff}}(\mathbf{f})  for each functional requirement vector  \mathbf{f} . If any  R_{\text{eff}} < r_{\text{min}} , targeted training or AI knowledge replication (with irreplicability multiplier  \alpha(v) ) is mandated.

7.2 AI Irreplicability and Hybrid Criticality

The criticality index from earlier drafts is generalised to the multiplex Hilbert framework:

Definition 7.1 (Weighted Hybrid Criticality).
For each agent  v , let  \mathrm{bc}(v)  be the betweenness centrality in the effective communication layer, and  \alpha(v) \in [0,1]  the irreplicability factor ( \alpha = 1  for humans,  \alpha \ll 1  for AI agents whose knowledge can be perfectly copied). The criticality is

\tilde{\chi}(v) = \alpha(v) \cdot \mathrm{bc}(v) \cdot \sum_{\mathbf{f} \in \mathcal{F}} \mathbb{1}\!\left[ \langle \mathbf{k}_v, \mathbf{f} \rangle \ge \theta \land R_{\text{eff}}(\mathbf{f}) \le 2 \right],

where  \theta  is a competence threshold. Nodes with high  \tilde{\chi}  are single points of cognitive failure, and their loss triggers immediate redundancy-recovery actions.

