Appendix D. Proof of Theorem 3.3 (Error Amplification Bound)

Let A be the adjacency matrix of the directed delegation layer, and \rho(A) its spectral radius. The error vector at time t satisfies \mathbf{e}^{(t)} = A^t \mathbf{e}^{(0)}. By the bound \| \mathbf{e}^{(t)} \|_2 \le \| A^t \|_2 \| \mathbf{e}^{(0)} \|_2. For any matrix, \|A^t\|_2 \le C_\epsilon (\rho(A) + \epsilon)^t for any \epsilon>0, with constant C_\epsilon depending on the basis of eigenvectors (Gelfand's formula). Thus, for large t and any \delta>0, \| \mathbf{e}^{(t)} \|_2 \le C (\rho(A) + \delta)^t \| \mathbf{e}^{(0)} \|_2. If \rho(A) < 1, errors decay exponentially; if \rho(A) \ge 1, they can be amplified. This completes the proof. \square

