Appendix G. Proof of Lemma 6.2 (Structural Divergence and Stability)

Definition G.1 (Structural divergence).
Let L_{\text{perf}} and L_{\text{obs}} be the normalised Laplacians of the reference and observed effective communication graphs. The structural divergence is

\mathcal{D} = \| L_{\text{perf}} - L_{\text{obs}} \|_F,

where \|\cdot\|_F is the Frobenius norm.

Lemma G.2 (Eigenvalue perturbation). For any two symmetric matrices X, Y,

\sum_{i=1}^{n} (\lambda_i(X) - \lambda_i(Y))^2 \le \| X - Y \|_F^2.

(Hoffman–Wielandt inequality). In particular, |\lambda_i(X) - \lambda_i(Y)| \le \| X - Y \|_F for each i.

Proof of Lemma 6.2.
Set X = L_{\text{perf}}, Y = L_{\text{obs}}. Then |\lambda_2(L_{\text{obs}}) - \lambda_2(L_{\text{perf}})| \le \mathcal{D}. If \lambda_2(L_{\text{perf}}) > \epsilon_{\text{crit}} + \tau, then by choosing \tau = (\lambda_2(L_{\text{perf}}) - \epsilon_{\text{crit}})/2 and enforcing \mathcal{D} \le \tau, we guarantee \lambda_2(L_{\text{obs}}) > \epsilon_{\text{crit}}. Similarly, for the spectral radius of the adjacency matrix of the delegation layer, which is a non-symmetric matrix, we use the bound |\rho(A_{\text{obs}}) - \rho(A_{\text{perf}})| \le \|A_{\text{obs}} - A_{\text{perf}}\|_2 \le \|A_{\text{obs}} - A_{\text{perf}}\|_F. Thus if the Frobenius divergence of the adjacency matrices is also bounded, \rho(A) stays within safe limits. Hence a combined Frobenius bound on both Laplacian and adjacency differences yields joint stability. \square

